# AG - Cyrus one-account bridge: cyrus.my + nxeon.cloud (r36, 2026-10-11)
Branch `feature/cyrus-r36-bridge` (worktree `/tank/dev-worktrees/cyrus-r36`, from r2, latest r2 `29cbc822dd` merged). NOT merged into r2, NOT deployed, no migration, no flag flipped, nginx/DNS untouched. With `CYRUS_DOMAIN_MODE` unset nothing changes.

## Commits
1. `fdb0c1e78b` dual-host shell: middleware + `lib/cyrus/bridge/{config,routing}.ts`; cyrus.my gets the Cyrus brand bar (`components/cyrus/host-shell`) around the SAME `/dashboard/cyrus` pages; portal pages hand off to Nxeon; the rest 404s.
2. `30ce5b5224` SSO: Sign in with Nxeon (Ed25519 assertion, state/nonce, single-use, exact redirect_uri), sign-up via Nxeon /register behind a consent screen, verified email, id-only matching, own Cyrus cookie/token type parented to the Nxeon session, impersonation never crosses, Sign in with Cyrus, signed logout hop, rate limits.
3. `f765028559` purchase -> credit: card checkouts return to the host they started on; wallet top-ups (idempotent charge by reference, compensating refund, pending/failed states, reconcile, refunds reverse unspent tokens); signed purchase webhook sender (Nxeon side) + receiver (Cyrus side), idempotent.
4. `5f976b87fc` + `3c23bfa9d2` two-origin e2e + fixes it found (rewrite target, absolute redirects, strict verified email, CSP form-action), docs. Merge `09142bbb09`.

## Ran (node-2 via devhost)
- `tsc --noEmit` clean after the final merge; full Cyrus suite **2310/2310**; host seam ratchet passes (no new Nxeon imports under lib/cyrus).
- DB test (throwaway `wt_cyrus_r36`): 6/6 (wallet once on retry, insufficient funds, failed credit refunds, signed receiver + redelivery, reconcile, refund).
- **Two-origin e2e** (`next dev`, cyrus.my and nxeon.cloud via `curl --resolve`, per-host jars): mode on **46/46** (one transient failure on an earlier run right after a hot reload, then clean twice); mode off **6/6** (no studio on cyrus.my, no IdP, internal tree 404, spoofed marker ignored, Nxeon dashboard + login unchanged).

## Security review (own flow)
Checked: open redirect (exact redirect_uri, validated next, configured origins only), login CSRF (nonce bound to the starting browser), replay (state consumed, jti once), forged subject (signature), header spoofing (marker stripped), impersonation leak (refused at authorize, ignored on cyrus.my), session fixation (fresh cookie), consent CSRF (Origin + bound token), logout CSRF (POST + Origin; Nxeon hop needs a signed token), back-channel (parent revocation), staff (no reverse SSO for staff/2FA), CSP form-action (fixed). Residual: replay caches, rate limits, the wallet lock and the outbox are per process; the assertion sits in a URL for up to 120 s (useless without the browser's state cookie); no-JS password login has Kodely's same form-action limit.

## Not done
- No wallet button in the tokens modal (API only); card purchases credit directly, not via the event path.
- Not run: `next build`, Playwright/real browser, real Stripe, staging under nginx + `next start` (dev needed `-H localhost` for internal rewrites).
- Owner list: `OWNER-ACTIONS.md` "r36" (nginx paths, env, Stripe domain, cookie/logout/verification defaults, SQL proposals, legal copy).
# AI - Cyrus bridge: Connect Cyrus + Nxeon Platform API (r38, 2026-10-11)
Branch `feature/cyrus-r38-bridge-api` (worktree `/tank/dev-worktrees/cyrus-r38`, from r2, latest r2 `1e20a0978a` merged). NOT merged into r2, NOT deployed, no migration run, no flag flipped. Defaults assumed: Nxeon = identity + wallet + payment provider; per-server grants; Cyrus never gets SSH.

## Commits
1. `08d09b7d5b` Connect Cyrus consent screen `/dashboard/connect/cyrus`, grants (7 scopes, revoke), memory + SQL stores, SQL proposal `prisma/manual-migration-cyrus-bridge-grants.sql`.
2. `a7aa53413c` Platform API v1 `/api/platform/cyrus/v1/*`: servers, inventory (incl. Mods-tab records), file primitives (allow-list, 64 MiB caps, sha preconditions), reload, budgeted restart, log tail, pack.set; HMAC + Cyrus-signed Ed25519 user assertion + grant per call; rate limits, idempotency, audit; rollback-only window after revoke. Cyrus client + `createHttpHost({ platform })` + delivery session over the primitives. OpenAPI generated + pinned.
3. `dccf08c4a3` Entitlements: plans/tokens as Nxeon products, `GET /entitlements`, signed `entitlement.changed`, Cyrus mirror (60 s cache, fail closed), reconciliation, refunds/chargebacks reverse once, partner hook (off).
4. `70cf992934` Events: change watcher (`server.version_changed`, `server.deleted` revokes grants), `server.restarted`, `grant.*`; Cyrus handlers (outdated -> SERVERS_AHEAD alert); wired build.finished, mod.published, install.result, delivery.rolledback.
5. `e0a5775e2a` UX: "Create a mod for this server" prefill; "Install to server" pre-install conflict report (Mods-tab duplicates block) in InstallModal + ShipBar.
6. `08939b5741` e2e + real flight + fixes + docs. Merge `044830d00e`.

## Ran (node-2 via devhost)
- `tsc --noEmit` clean; full Cyrus suite **2375/2375**; host seam + db-split ratchets pass (Cyrus tables via `cyrusDb` only).
- DB tests (throwaway `wt_cyrus_r38`, SQL proposal applied there only): 12/12 (mirror, fail-closed gate, pull, purchases once, refund + chargeback once, SQL grant store + outbox).
- Two-service e2e: 5/5 (fresh install, revoke mid-install, revoke mid-update, broken worldgen rollback with 2 budgeted restarts, no/read-only grant).
- **Real node-2 run** (`bridge-r38-flight-2026-10-11.json`): A delivered through 120 API calls (69 changes), one real Paper 1.21.11 Test Flight boot **passed** (boot, plugins, log clean, rcon, clean stop), health ok. R: revoke mid-update -> rolled back, **exact restore**, 1 forward refusal. The first run found a real bug (rollback re-creating an existing parent folder was refused -> rollback_incomplete); fixed, re-run clean. Throwaway dir removed.

## Fixed on the way
r36 purchase receiver dropped a failed event as a duplicate; purchase sender never flushed; tokens sweep would have sent mirrored plans to Stripe.

## Not done / not run
- No `next build`, no browser/Playwright of the consent page, buttons or reports.
- No real Nxeon server touched (fake Nxeon + Test Flight only); no real Stripe/dispute call.
- Memory stores/caches per process; card top-ups not in the snapshot; `library.contributed` unemitted; partner attribution computes a proposal only.

Owner list: `OWNER-ACTIONS.md` "r38" (SQL, consent copy, keys, flag order, chargeback + partner decisions).
     1	import { NextRequest, NextResponse } from "next/server";
     2	import NXM_LIVE_ROUTES from "./app/nxm/_data/live-routes.json";
     3	import { anonModCacheControl } from "./lib/seo-cache";
     4	import { bridgeConfig, isCyrusHost, CYRUS_HOST_HEADER } from "./lib/cyrus/bridge/config";
