    14	// Every file actually committed under public/ -- logos, game art, flags,
    15	// brand assets, blog images, docs, fonts. None of it is per-customer or
    16	// sensitive; it's already served unauthenticated at the same path on the
    17	// main site, so exposing it on the admin/staff hosts too doesn't defeat the
    18	// isolation below (that's about app pages like /dashboard, not static
    19	// files). Without this, every <img> under public/ 404s on the admin/staff
